---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Accessibility Statement | The Scroll of Dharma';
const description = 'Our commitment to digital accessibility and WCAG 2.1 AA compliance';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="parchment-card">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mb-6 text-center">
        Accessibility Statement
      </h1>
      
      <div class="prose prose-amber max-w-none space-y-6 font-body text-amber-900">
        <section>
          <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
            The Scroll of Dharma is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. 
            We continually improve the user experience for everyone and apply relevant accessibility standards 
            to ensure our content is accessible to all.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Our Commitment
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            We strive to conform to the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/" 
            class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web 
            Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1</a> at Level AA. These guidelines explain how to make 
            web content more accessible for people with disabilities and improve usability for all users.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Accessibility Features
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Scroll of Dharma includes the following accessibility features:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li><strong>Semantic HTML:</strong> Proper use of HTML5 semantic elements for clear document structure</li>
            <li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> All interactive elements are fully keyboard accessible</li>
            <li><strong>Screen Reader Support:</strong> ARIA labels and semantic markup for screen reader compatibility</li>
            <li><strong>Alternative Text:</strong> Descriptive alt text for all images and SVG illustrations</li>
            <li><strong>Color Contrast:</strong> Text and interactive elements meet WCAG AA contrast ratios (4.5:1 minimum)</li>
            <li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Mobile-first design that adapts to different screen sizes and zoom levels</li>
            <li><strong>Focus Indicators:</strong> Visible focus indicators on all interactive elements</li>
            <li><strong>Audio Transcripts:</strong> Text alternatives for all narrative audio content</li>
            <li><strong>Reduced Motion:</strong> Respect for <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> user preference</li>
            <li><strong>Clear Navigation:</strong> Consistent navigation structure with breadcrumbs</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Standards Compliance
          </h2>
          <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-700 p-4 mb-4">
            <p class="font-semibold">WCAG 2.1 Level AA Compliant</p>
            <p class="text-sm mt-2">
              As of December 2025, The Scroll of Dharma conforms to WCAG 2.1 Level AA standards.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            We have conducted thorough accessibility audits and continue to monitor and improve our compliance. 
            Our commitment extends to maintaining these standards as we add new content and features.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Technical Specifications
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            This website is built with accessibility in mind using:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li><strong>Astro:</strong> Static site generator for fast, accessible page loads</li>
            <li><strong>TypeScript:</strong> Type-safe code for reliability</li>
            <li><strong>Semantic HTML5:</strong> Proper markup for assistive technologies</li>
            <li><strong>ARIA Attributes:</strong> Enhanced accessibility information where needed</li>
            <li><strong>Native HTML Controls:</strong> Standard audio and navigation controls</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Compatibility
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Scroll of Dharma is designed to be compatible with:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>Recent versions of major browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)</li>
            <li>Screen readers including NVDA, JAWS, and VoiceOver</li>
            <li>Mobile devices running iOS and Android</li>
            <li>Browser zoom levels up to 200%</li>
            <li>Keyboard-only navigation</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Known Limitations
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            While we strive for full accessibility, we acknowledge the following limitations:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4 mb-4">
            <li>Some SVG animations may not fully respect reduced-motion preferences</li>
            <li>Audio content for "Birth of Dharma" chapter is still in production</li>
            <li>Complex visual illustrations may not convey all details in text descriptions</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            We are actively working to address these limitations in upcoming releases.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Feedback and Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            We welcome your feedback on the accessibility of The Scroll of Dharma. If you encounter 
            accessibility barriers, please let us know:
          </p>
          <div class="bg-parchment-100 border border-amber-700/30 rounded-lg p-4 space-y-2">
            <p><strong>Contact Methods:</strong></p>
            <ul class="list-none space-y-2 ml-4">
              <li>
                📧 <strong>Email:</strong> 
                <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/issues" 
                   class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">
                  Open an issue on GitHub
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                💬 <strong>Discussion:</strong> 
                <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/discussions" 
                   class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">
                  Start a discussion on GitHub
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                📝 <strong>Report:</strong> 
                Include the page URL, the issue encountered, and your assistive technology (if applicable)
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
            We aim to respond to accessibility feedback within 3-5 business days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Accessibility Resources
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Additional accessibility documentation:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
            <li>
              <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/blob/main/ACCESSIBILITY_AUDIT.md" 
                 class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">
                Accessibility Audit Report
              </a> - Detailed findings and improvements
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/blob/main/docs/AUDIO_TRANSCRIPTS.md" 
                 class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">
                Audio Transcripts
              </a> - Complete text alternatives for all audio content
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" 
                 class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">
                Contributing Guide
              </a> - Accessibility standards for contributors
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Continuous Improvement
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Accessibility is an ongoing effort. We regularly:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4 mb-4">
            <li>Conduct accessibility audits on new features</li>
            <li>Test with assistive technologies</li>
            <li>Gather user feedback from the disability community</li>
            <li>Update our accessibility documentation</li>
            <li>Train contributors on accessibility best practices</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            Our <a href="https://github.com/saint2706/scroll-of-dharma/blob/main/ROADMAP_2025-2027.md" 
                   class="text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-900 underline">strategic roadmap</a> includes 
            plans for WCAG 2.1 Level AAA compliance and ongoing accessibility excellence initiatives.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-heading font-bold text-amber-900 mt-8 mb-4">
            Formal Complaints
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            If you are not satisfied with our response to your accessibility concerns, you may escalate 
            the issue through GitHub's accessibility reporting channels or contact relevant disability 
            rights organizations in your jurisdiction.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-amber-700/30">
          <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 italic text-center">
            <strong>Last Updated:</strong> December 2025<br/>
            <strong>Next Review:</strong> June 2026
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 text-center mt-4">
            This accessibility statement applies to <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} 
            class="underline">https://saint2706.github.io/scroll-of-dharma</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a 
          href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}
          class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-amber-100 hover:bg-amber-200 border border-amber-700/40 rounded-lg font-heading text-amber-900 transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          ← Return to Home
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    color: inherit;
  }
  
  .prose a {
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  
  .prose code {
    background-color: rgb(254 243 199 / 0.5);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.875em;
  }
  
  .prose strong {
    color: rgb(120 53 15);
  }
</style>
